## Browser gate runs

- Run 1: `bash apps/storytime/__tests__/phase3-browser-gate.sh`. Exit 1; `PASS=3, FAIL=1`.
- Run 2: the same command. Exit 1; `PASS=3, FAIL=1`.
- Both runs end the same way before any app row:
  - `PASS: Production build exits 0`
  - `PASS: Ready clone uses shipped w01 with approvals and placeholder media`
  - `PASS: Built server answers HTTP 200`
  - `FAIL: Playwright gate exits 1`
  - `PASS=3, FAIL=1`
- The Playwright script crashes at once:
  - `browserContext.newCDPSession: Protocol error (Target.attachToTarget): No target with given id found`
  - `at watchNetwork (apps/storytime/.next/phase3-browser-gate-<pid>.mjs:24:30)`
  - `at apps/storytime/.next/phase3-browser-gate-<pid>.mjs:62:27`
- No labeled app line is printed, because the gate prints the result array at the end.

## Root cause

- `phase3-browser-gate.sh` line 107: `const cdp = page.context().newCDPSession(page);` inside `function watchNetwork(page)` at line 102.
- `newCDPSession` returns a `Promise`. A local probe prints `constructor=Promise`, `typeof cdp.on=undefined`, `typeof cdp.send=undefined`.
- Lines 109, 114, and 118 therefore call `.on` and `.send` on a Promise. Under `heavy-run.sh` the unhandled attach rejection crashes Node with the CDP error above. Outside `heavy-run.sh` the crash is `cdp.on is not a function`.
- This is a harness defect in the Red retry. It is not an app defect.

## Verified fix for Mid Red

- Line 102: `async function watchNetwork(page) {`.
- Line 107: `const cdp = await page.context().newCDPSession(page);`.
- Proof: a probe of the same awaited call under `heavy-run.sh` attaches a CDP session and enables the Network domain 3 of 3 times, with the default 3G memory scope and `channel: 'chrome'`.

